  "full_text": "The main reason I was chosen to make Temple OS is to it takes let's say 100 lines of C C++ to get something done today. 10 years ago it took 50 lines. 20 years ago it took 10 lines. In order to do simple things they've been making it more and more complicated. And what TempleOS is, you know how there's a 1040EZ tax form and there's a 1040 tax form? What is the purpose of the 1040EZ? Why do we have the 1040EZ when there's a 1040? Okay, well, it's simpler. That's the purpose. A lot of people... For a long time, we all thought that compatibility was really great. Yeah, it's really nice. We want everybody doing the same. Okay, well, it's reached a point where this is a 1040EZ and the other is the 1040. Okay, so is it a replacement? No. Okay, so here's the deal. A lot of people are going to say, you need to do it like this. And I say, dude, that's called the 1040, okay? I get where you're coming from. You're coming from the 1040, okay? You're kind of a little bit retarded. You're kind of retarded. If you tell me to make the 1040 easy, more like the 1040, I'm going, okay, okay. I fully understand what you're trying to tell me. I'm telling you, no, hell no, okay? Fuck yourself, retard. The person's like, yep, but look, you really need to. I'm going, dude, dude, dude, 1040EZ, okay? Hell no. Fuck yourself, okay? You're a fucking retard. Now, why is this? This is the, fuck it. I'm going to do one thing and one thing only. There was a famous Renaissance artist. I think he was trying to get a job with the Pope or something. And what he did is he drew a circle. And that was his job interview. Okay. Fuck you. End of story. I win. In your fucking face, okay?",
